    "title": "Italy survives Northern Ireland in World Cup playoff: Highlights",
    "text": "5:38 pm ET March 26, 2026FINAL - Italy 2-0 Northern IrelandThat's it! Italy moves on to the final on Sunday after a nervy, but ultimately comfortable win.5:26 pm ET March 26, 202680' - Italy 2-0 Northern IrelandGOAL ITALY! Kean has just about put the game away for the hosts! The forward takes down a long ball in the box with his right foot, cuts onto his left and buries a shot into the far post.5:11 pm ET March 26, 202664' - Italy 1-0 Northern IrelandItaly makes its first two changes, with Bastoni and Retegui coming off and replaced by Gatti and Esposito.5:01 pm ET March 26, 202656' - Italy 1-0 Northern IrelandGOAL ITALY! Tonali gives his side a huge lead! A clearance falls right to the Newcastle midfielder's feet, and he fires a first-time low drive home.4:51 pm ET March 26, 202646' - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandWe are underway in the second half!4:48 pm ET March 26, 2026Halftime scores across EuropeCzech Republic 1-2 Republic of Ireland (Schik; Parrott, Kovar OG)Denmark 0-0 North MacedoniaItaly 0-0 Northern IrelandPoland 0-1 Albania(Hoxha)Slovakia 2-1 Kosovo (Valjent, Haraslin; Hodza)Ukraine 0-1 Sweden (Gyokeres)Wales 0-0 Bosnia and Herzegovina4:34 pm ET March 26, 2026HT - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandThats the end of a nervy first half in Bergamo. Italy has been the better team but hasn't caused too much danger.4:30 pm ET March 26, 202634' - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandHandball shout for Italy off a corner but it comes to nothing, as the Northern Ireland defender looked to have his arm tucked against his body.4:19 pm ET March 26, 202630' - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandItaly hasn't been as dangerous in the last 5-10 minutes, losing some of its threat from earlier. In the meantime, the visitors have looked to exploit a back line that hasn't looked entirely robust.4:08 pm ET March 26, 202620' - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandItaly well on top so far as expected, with five shots to Northern Ireland's zero and 65 percent possession. Northern Ireland has looked like it can cause danger on the counter, however.3:59 pm ET March 26, 20268' - Italy 0-0 Northern IrelandSome early pressure by Italy, with Federico Dimarco forcing a good near-post save from Pierce Charles after a deflected cross.3:47 pm ET March 26, 2026Kickoff!We are underway in Bergamo.3:40 pm ET March 26, 2026European playoffs todayHere are the seven simultaneous kickoffs across Europe at 3:45 p.m. ET.Slovakia vs. KosovoItaly vs. Northern IrelandWales vs. Bosnia and HerzegovinaUkraine vs. SwedenPoland vs. AlbaniaDenmark vs. North MacedoniaCzechia vs. Ireland3:37 pm ET March 26, 2026Turkey beats RomaniaIn the first game of the day, Turkey defeated Romania 1-0 to advance to the final, where it will face Slovakia or Kosovo.3:15 pm ET March 26, 2026Northern Ireland lineup vs. Italy3:05 pm ET March 26, 2026Italy lineup vs. Northern Ireland3:00 pm ET March 26, 2026Northern Ireland roster vs. ItalyGoalkeepers: Bailey Peacock-Farrell (Blackpool, on loan from Birmingham City), Conor Hazard (Plymouth Argyle), Pierce Charles (Sheffield Wednesday), Josh Clarke (Partick Thistle, on loan from Celtic).Defenders: Tom Atcheson (Blackburn Rovers), Trai Hume (Sunderland), Ciaron Brown and Brodie Spencer (both Oxford United), Paddy McNair (Hull City), Eoin Toal (Bolton Wanderers), Ruairi McConville (Norwich City), Terry Devlin (Portsmouth).Midfielders: Jamie Donley and Jamie McDonnell (both Oxford United), George Saville (Luton Town), Alistair McCann (Preston North End), Shea Charles (Southampton), Isaac Price (West Bromwich Albion), Paul Smyth (Queens Park Rangers), Ethan Galbraith (Swansea City), Justin Devenny (Crystal Palace), Brad Lyons (Kilmarnock), Patrick Kelly (Barnsley), Kieran Morrison (Liverpool).Forwards: Josh Magennis (Exeter City), Dion Charles (Huddersfield Town), Callum Marshall (Vfl Bochum, on loan from West Ham United), Jamie Reid (Stevenage)2:55 pm ET March 26, 2026Italy roster vs. Northern IrelandGoalkeepers: Elia Caprile (Cagliari), Marco Carnesecchi (Atalanta), Gianluigi Donnarumma (Manchester City), Alex Meret (Napoli).Defenders: Alessandro Bastoni (Inter), Alessandro Buongiorno (Napoli), Riccardo Calafiori (Arsenal), Andrea Cambiaso (Juventus), Diego Coppola (Paris FC), Federico Dimarco (Inter), Federico Gatti (Juventus), Gianluca Mancini (Roma), Marco Palestra (Cagliari), Giorgio Scalvini (Atalanta), Leonardo Spinazzola (Napoli).Midfielders: Nicolo Barella (Inter), Bryan Cristante (Roma), Davide Frattesi (Inter), Manuel Locatelli (Juventus), Niccolo Pisilli (Roma), Sandro Tonali (Newcastle).Forwards: Nicolo Cambiaghi (Bolonga), Francesco Pio Esposito (Inter), Moise Kean (Fiorentina), Matteo Politano (Napoli), Giacomo Raspadori (Atalanta), Mateo Retegui (Al-Qadsiah), Gianluca Scamacca (Atalanta).2:50 pm ET March 26, 2026Italy vs. Northern Ireland channel, start time, streamingWhen: Thursday, March 26Where: Stadio di Bergamo (Bergamo, Italy)Time: 3:45 p.m. ETChannel/streaming: ViX (Watch on Prime Video)2:44 pm ET March 26, 2026Welcome!Welcome to USA TODAY's live coverage of today's massive UEFA World Cup qualifying playoff between Italy and Northern Ireland. Follow along for updates throughout the match.",
